message.content:
Below is a minimal example of a “flip‑card” that rotates (around the Y‑axis) when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the HTML and CSS into your project and tweak the dimensions, colors, or animation speed as you like.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Hover‑Rotate Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣  Container ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣  Card (front & back) ---------- */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* Needed for 3D children */
  transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* Smooth rotation */
}

.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* Rotate on hover */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣  Front side ---------- */
.card .front,
.card .back {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide backside when flipped */
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

.card .front {
  background: #fff;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #333;
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣  Back side ---------- */
.card .back {
  background: #f8f8f8;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);    /* Start rotated so it’s hidden */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: #555;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="front">
      Front Side
    </div>
    <div class="back">
      Back Side
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| 1 | `perspective` on the wrapper | Creates a 3‑D space so the rotation looks realistic. |
| 2 | `transform-style: preserve-3d` on `.card` | Keeps child elements in 3‑D space. |
| 3 | `backface-visibility: hidden` on front/back | Hides the backside when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| 4 | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on hover | Rotates the card 180° around the Y‑axis. |
| 5 | `transition` on `.card` | Smoothly animates the rotation. |

You can change `rotateY` to `rotateX` if you prefer a vertical flip, or adjust the `transition` duration to make it faster/slower. Enjoy!
